            <ArticleTitle>Analysis of vessel wall morphology, blood flow velocity, and the hemostatic system in a patient with a large intracoronary thrombus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>298-305</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with AMI caused by a large thrombus in the proximal LAD was successfully treated with PTCA and an intracoronary lysis combined with the platelet-receptor antagonist c7E3. Analysis of cellular hemostasis after 1 and 6 months revealed a sustained platelet activation despite combined anti-platelet therapy with ASA and ticlopidine. A progredient slow-flow phenomenon appeared during control angiographies, confirmed by intracoronary Doppler examination.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
